{"name":"Goose Feathers","hex":"#d2cdc4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various grazing waterfowl of the family Anatidae, which have feathers and webbed feet and are capable of flying, swimming, and walking on land, and which are generally bigger than ducks.","A female goose."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sharply poke or pinch the buttocks, or prod between the buttocks (of a person).","To stimulate; to spur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goose"},{"term":"feathers","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of feather"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of feather"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feathers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Goose","blocks":[{"text":"A goose is a bird of any of several waterfowl species in the family Anatidae. This group comprises the genera Anser and Branta. Some members of the Tadorninae subfamily are commonly called geese, but are not considered \"true geese\" taxonomically. More distantly related members of the family Anatidae are swans, most of which are larger than true geese, and ducks, which are smaller."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goose","wikidata":"Q16529344"},{"title":"Feather","blocks":[{"text":"Feathers are epidermal growths that form a distinctive outer covering, or plumage, on both avian (bird) and some non-avian dinosaurs and other archosaurs. They are the most complex integumentary structures found in vertebrates and an example of a complex evolutionary novelty. They are among the characteristics that distinguish the extant birds from other living groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg/330px-Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather","wikidata":"Q81025"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/500px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/1280px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg/500px-Anser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Snow geese (Anser caerulescens) in Quebec, Canada","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnser_caerulescens_CT8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/500px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/1280px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG/500px-B%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chinese geese (Anser cygnoides domesticus), the domesticated form of the swan goose (Anser cygnoides)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AB%C3%BCtyk%C3%B6s_l%C3%BAd_-_Gergelyiugornya.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/c